{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1554386-what-can-a-spetre-in-catharsis-do","id":1554386,"title":"What can a Spetre in Catharsis do","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-10-15T22:50:55-07:00","id":1554386,"title":"What can a Spetre in Catharsis do","content":"Ideas beyond attacking its comrades?<br /> <br /> if you were a spectre in catharsis and had info that needs to get into wraithly hands immediately ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 10-17-2025, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T10:51:18-07:00","id":1554599,"title":"","content":"Depends on the Spectre, the situation, and in many cases, on how good the Psyche is at subtlety. Most wraiths aren't likely to believe that a Spectre is in catharsis just because it says so. The Psyche will either have to hide the fact that it is a Spectre, prove that it is in Catharsis, or manipulate Wraiths into believing the information regardless. A good example of that last one giving the information in a way that looks like the Spectre is actually trying to withhold it.<br /> <br /> What options the Cathartic Spectre has will depend on the kind of Spectre.<br /> <br /> Mortwights are not in a great position to share information. They can potentially pass for wraiths if they can keep their death wounds hidden. This is easier in the Shadowlands but they have limited time to act there, it is harder in the Tempest where they are constantly bleeding. They also aren't likely to know much unless they have the skill to pull it directly from the Hive Mind. Their rank is so low that other Spectres aren't likely to just volunteer information unless it is necessary.<br /> <br /> If they do know something important, often their best option is going to be to act like an overeager Spectre. They can warn of an impending attack by making threats about what they are going to do to the Wraiths during it, for instance. A clever Mortwight could also weave important information into a harrowing by pulling in the right &quot;matter and memories&quot; as Wr20 puts it.<br /> <hr /><br /> Dopplegangers are likely the best situated to feed information to Wraiths. Many of them still have the position in Wraith society they had before they fell, which means they likely have at least some Wraiths who do not know they are Spectres and who trust them. As long as they have a reasonable story about how they know the information, they can probably get it into helpful hands easily enough.<br /> <br /> The real issue for Dopplegangers is having the information in the first place. You can think of Dopplegangers hiding in Wraith society as deep cover agents. If the faction of Spectres they are working with has any kind of information security, they aren't told more than they need to be. They will have information that pertains to their current goals, whatever they are, but not much beyond that unless they've gone looking for it.<br /> <hr /><br /> Nephwracks are very likely to have a lot of sensitive information. They are also very obviously twisted Spectres with no hope of passing for a normal Wraith and are also likely surrounded by other Spectres. If they are convincing enough to persuade the Wraiths that they are in Catharsis, they will also be convincing enough to persuade any nearby Spectres and that won't go well. In fact the most likely scenario is that they convince the Spectres and not the Wraiths. Wraiths aren't likely to believe a Nephwrack. Even &quot;accidentally&quot; dropped information is likely to be met with suspicion.<br /> <br /> A Cathartic Nephwrack who really wants to get information out is going to need the Wraiths to think they uncovered that information themselves, either by setting them on a path to finding it, or letting them &quot;trick&quot; him into revealing it. It couldn't hurt to put on a good show of trying to keep the Wraiths from escaping with it once they have it.<br /> <hr /><br /> The typical Shade has been stripped of personality and intellect. They rarely have the capacity to understand or recognize vital information and even if they are capable of Catharsis, it is likely the Psyche has the same limitations.<br /> <br /> Hekatonkhires are in a similar situation as far as I am aware.<br /> <hr /><br /> Pasiphae do not enter Catharsis any more than Ferrymen do. <br /> <hr /><br /> It honestly never occured to me until now that the Onceborn could enter Catharsis. If it did happen, the knowledge they could give would be vast, but the opportunity to do so directly almost nonexistent unless there is already a Wraith in their presence. Their best option is to direct their various forces in such a way that they create openings for any vital information to be discovered. They have to do this, though, without it looking like a weakness or a misstep because the other Onceborn are watching and ready to pounce.<br /> <hr /><br /> The Neverborn were never human and there is no indication they are split into Shadow and Psyche. As such there is no reason to think there is a Psyche that could take over. If it did, it would be just as alien as the Shadow so I'm not sure it would even think of talking to Wraiths as an option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-24T07:53:58-07:00","id":1554640,"title":"","content":"The Psyche has four main motivations in Catharsis.<br /> <br /> 1) Redeem itself. It wants to claw back control permanently and it may take steps to advance that goal if it can see any.<br /> <br /> 2) Engage in Passions. This is really part of the first goal, but the Psyche could just try to fulfill these for Pathos and solace, so it gets its own entry.<br /> <br /> 3) Interfere with the Shadow's goals and relationships. I can see this easily being a trap for an unwary Psyche as it wastes its energy on short term victories. Nevertheless, a Psyche can gain a lot by isolating the Shadow from the support of its 'friends' in the Hive Mind. He has to be careful though, because...<br /> <br /> 4) Survive. This is the big one. Catharsis for Psyche's can be quite a tightrope walk because they have a motivation the Shadow doesn't. They want to survive. The Shadow wants to go into Oblivion. It may have other things it wants to do first, but it always wants Oblivion. So a Shadow in control during a Wraith's Catharsis is willing to risk a lot more than a Psyche in control during a Shadow's.<br /> <br /> That last one is critical because it means many Psyches do not want to admit vulnerability (like Catharsis) in front of Spectres or Wraiths.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, how a Psyche can take advantage of Catharsis is going to vary greatly on the individual Spectre and on things like Dark Passions and temperament.<br /> Consider a Spectre with a Dark Passion: Be Honest, Especially When it Hurts (Twisted Love). That's not an unreasonably Dark Passion and it means that this Spectre may already be inclined to give information away. He may be the kind to stand at the edge of Hierarchy territory and scream threats of upcoming attacks to watch Wraith's squirm.<br /> <br /> It also means that when the Psyche gives away information when it is in control, it will feed that Dark Passion. Those don't go away in Catharsis, after all. Instead, if the Psyche knows anything his Shadow hasn't already shouted to all and sundry, he will want to manipulate it into the right hands.<br /> <br /> But another tactic he might use is picking at the emotional weak points of his 'allies'. Now that will likely give them Angst but two things about that. First, Angst sucks and though Spectres are energized by that pain it doesn't mean they like it. It it is painful enough being around the character, they may well avoid him. Second, Spectres crave Oblivion and Angst is connected to that. It is possible, though not at all certain, to drive Spectres into Oblivion with enough pain. I see this as very likely to backfire and drown the Psyche in Angst, but it is a tactic he might consider.<br /> <br /> If he really does his research, he could even feed the Passions of his 'allies.' Spectres are also likely to avoid things that make their consciences start jumping up and down. If they do, he isolates his Shadow, and if they don't he may make allies of the other Psyches. Of course, he has to remember to do this through lies and manipulation or he may still feed his own Shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T15:55:59-08:00","id":1554990,"title":"","content":"something I just thought of safe to say that the line from chrono triggers princess schala &quot;I know that you cant forgive her but please dont hate her&quot; is representive of a psyche dominated spectre","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 11-02-2025, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name"